// TEST: While On Ordinary Match Arm (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// `while` belongs to the recursive-array arm and only there: it declares when
// the INDUCTION stops (and the array freezes). An ordinary match arm has no
// induction to stop -- its guard is `if`, and a failing `if` falls through to
// the next arm -- so the two clauses are not interchangeable in either
// direction. The mirror case (`if` on a rec-array arm) steers back the other
// way, in recursive-arrays/014's neighbourhood.
//
// The steer also has to SURVIVE the arm-list combinator: `many` treats any
// arm failure as "the list ends here", which used to discard this message and
// re-report the generic "Expected declaration but got '|'" at the next arm.

let x = 5
let r = match x with
    | n while n > 3 -> 1
    | _ -> 0
// ERROR: BL1003
// ERROR-CONTAINS: guards a RECURSIVE-ARRAY arm
